WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.568
-Our first guest tonight
is a talented actor

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:03.670
and comedian, you know,
from movies such as "Air,"

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.671
the "Rush Hour" films,
and "Friday."

00:00:05.671 --> 00:00:07.940
He's currently on his
Chris Tucker The Legend

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:09.108
stand-up tour.

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:10.276
You can see him
at the Beacon Theatre

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:12.312
here in New York,
November 17th and 18th.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.280
Tickets are available
at christucker.com.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.549
Please welcome to the show
Chris Tucker, everybody.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.718
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:36.669 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.404
-I like -- I like that.

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:40.406
Can y'all come and bring me
out tomorrow night

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.141
at the Beacon Theatre?

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:44.710
And the next night?
-There you go.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:45.912
They're great, right?
-They are awesome, man.

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.379
-You're great.
I'm so happy to have you here.

00:00:47.379 --> 00:00:49.115
-Man, I'm happy to be here, man.
-This is very --

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.550
I will say,
let me tell you something,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.785
because you've earned the right
to call yourself a legend.

00:00:52.785 --> 00:00:54.186
-Thank you, man.
-You have to have the confidence

00:00:54.186 --> 00:00:56.288
to put it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.288 --> 00:00:58.291
-You know, I thought people
was trying to say I was old.

00:00:58.291 --> 00:00:59.993
You know, younger people say,
"Man, you a legend."

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.294
I'm like, "I ain't that old,
man. Wait a minute."

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:04.096
And then I kind of accepted it.
-Yeah, you got to --

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:06.499
When they give you "Legend,"
you got to wear "Legend."

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:07.566
-You just take it.
-You got to take it.

00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:09.101
-Yeah.
-You're playing the Beacon.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:10.203
I know you've
played there before.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.037
It is a wonderful theater.
Are you excited?

00:01:12.037 --> 00:01:13.739
-I'm excited, man, I'm excited.

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:15.741
Last time I played there,
Harry Belafonte --

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:17.844
Harry Belafonte came and saw me,
and he said,

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:21.247
"Chris, you need to sing more."
And that's what I do in my show.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.783
I sing, I dance, I act,
I do it all.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.518
I tell jokes, I do it all.
So it's like --

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.288
it's like a Broadway play, man.
-You must be exhausted

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:30.389
at the end of it.
-You know what? I am.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:31.857
I am. It's like --
It's like, you know --

00:01:31.857 --> 00:01:34.026
It's like a racecar driver.
Formula 1 driver, man.

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:35.361
When I'm out there, in my show,

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.830
it's like, the energy
is coming at me.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:38.197
I'm giving it back to them.

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:39.765
So it's a lot of fun, man.
A lot of fun.

00:01:39.765 --> 00:01:41.935
-That's fantastic.
I know your last --

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.837
your last hour was on Netflix.
-Yeah.

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:46.372
You talked --
You're very honest

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.706
about things
that have happened in your life.

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:49.942
You're honest about tax
problems, things like that.

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:51.343
Is that still
what people can expect?

00:01:51.343 --> 00:01:52.612
That you are kind of laying it
out there?

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.913
-I talk about it all.
I talk about it all.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:55.948
I finally paid they butt off.
They had me on the road.

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:57.483
I told them --
I was like Tony Montana.

00:01:57.483 --> 00:01:58.718
I said, "Let me go out
on the road, okay?

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.053
I'll make a meal here,
a meal there.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.354
I'll get you the money.
Okay, mang?"

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.922
[ Laughter ]
"Take it easy, okay?

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.824
You gonna have a heart attack,
man. Calm down."

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:06.626
-That's great. And the --
-I did what I could on the side,

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.094
but I stay loyal to you, man.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.094 --> 00:02:10.429
-And the IRS
responded to that.

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:13.800
-They responded. It was the IRS
tour for a couple years.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.602
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.835
They're backstage,
waiting on their money.

00:02:16.835 --> 00:02:18.471
I said, "Y'all a trip."
-Yeah.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:20.773
Maybe they love the show, too.
-They did. They enjoyed it.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:24.443
-Now, you were the youngest
of six growing up in Atlanta.

00:02:24.443 --> 00:02:26.446
Do you feel like
being the youngest

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:27.881
gives you a head start
in comedy?

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:29.849
Because you just sort of,
like, grow up

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.884
and you've got
this older audience

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:34.087
that's already sort
of delighted by you?

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:35.788
-Oh, definitely, man.
You learn faster,

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.690
because you see --
you see your brothers

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.858
and sisters make mistakes,

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.860
and see my brothers
get a whupping.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.895
I'm like, "What you do?
God, dawg.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:45.197
Daddy tore your butt up."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:46.466
"I didn't take out the garbage.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.700
I got to make sure I take it out
when it's my turn."

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:48.901
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:51.137
-What day the garbage man come?
On Tuesday?

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.072
I got to remember that.
Yeah, all types of stuff, man.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.274
You learn, and then you
with their older friends.

00:02:55.274 --> 00:02:57.643
So you got to --
Then you can't say nothing.

00:02:57.643 --> 00:02:59.712
So you got to fight
your way into conversations.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.013
-Do you remember
the early things

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.414
that you were doing for jokes?

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:04.918
-Oh, well, I hosted
a high school talent show.

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.619
I talked about stuff.
I don't remember.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:08.687
I was just like a natural.
People would say I was funny,

00:03:08.687 --> 00:03:10.189
and I'd be like,
"What you talking about?"

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:12.158
They would say I remind them
of Eddie Murphy in high school.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.559
Then I hosted a talent show,

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.795
and I did it in,
you know, a stand-up form,

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.531
and I told my first school joke,
and I got a little laugh,

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.099
and I said, "Oh, I'mma do
this the rest of my life."

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.601
-Oh, I know, right?
-Best feeling in the world, man.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:22.735
-That first little itch,
and you're like,

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.337
"I'm never giving this up."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.871
You've had some incredible --

00:03:25.871 --> 00:03:28.374
Before you sort of
were leads in films,

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:32.578
you would just steal movies
with tiny little appearances.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.847
Johnny Booze.
-Oh, thank you, thank you.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.516
Thank you.
"House Party 3," yeah.

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:38.150
-"House Party 3."
-Yeah.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.553
-And Johnny Booze
kind of shows up,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.121
does his thing, and gets out.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:45.224
But a very --
a very memorable character.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:47.059
How much of Johnny Booze --
be honest --

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:48.594
was based on this outfit?

00:03:48.594 --> 00:03:49.796
-It was all of it.

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.130
Because when they gave me
the outfit, I said,

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.665
"Oh, God, he's a pimp
or something, so...

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:54.567
[ Laughter ]
"I'mma go ahead and do it."

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:56.369
And that came from stand-up,
you know, being ready.

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.470
Whatever they throw at you,

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.837
you get out there,
and you just do it.

00:03:58.837 --> 00:04:00.073
And I only had like
three minutes

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:03.609
to make my -- my mark,
you know, on that scene.

00:04:03.609 --> 00:04:05.111
So, yeah, the outfit helps.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:07.646
-Then, of course, "Friday."

00:04:07.646 --> 00:04:09.281
-"Friday," yeah. Yes.
Smokey.

00:04:09.281 --> 00:04:11.884
-Smokey.
-Smokey. Yeah.

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:14.787
-Anybody -- Did anybody
making this movie

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.322
have any sense of how long
a tail it would have,

00:04:17.322 --> 00:04:19.525
how people would just be
in love with it for years?

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.428
-Nobody knew. Nobody knew.
I remember me and Faizon Love,

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:24.429
who played Big Worm,
went and saw the movie.

00:04:24.429 --> 00:04:26.031
But it wasn't no score,
no music.

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:27.566
And we was like,
"Man, this is terrible, man.

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:29.268
We got to find another job."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:31.737
We didn't know, but I knew
that I did what I --

00:04:31.737 --> 00:04:33.973
You know, I was prepared,
I knew it was my shot.

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:36.008
You know, coming from
stand-up to acting,

00:04:36.008 --> 00:04:37.643
I had to, you know,
calm stuff down.

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:39.645
From stand-up, you're broad,
and acting,

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:40.946
you got to get
into the character.

00:04:40.946 --> 00:04:43.248
So I knew I got --
I got all that right.

00:04:43.248 --> 00:04:45.317
And when they put the score
and the music together,

00:04:45.317 --> 00:04:47.753
the director, Gary Gray, said,
"No, man, trust me, it's a hit.

00:04:47.753 --> 00:04:48.720
It's a good movie."

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:50.089
And we was like,
"Oh, we'll see."

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:52.424
And then it just became
what it became, so it's great.

00:04:52.424 --> 00:04:54.327
-Do people still yell things
from Smokey?

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:56.562
-Oh, "Smokey!"
They always yell, "Smokey!"

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.163
I'll be at church --
"Smokey!"

00:04:58.163 --> 00:04:59.398
Like, "Come on, man."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.398 --> 00:05:02.001
"Respect the Lord, man."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:03.135
"What's wrong with you?"

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:06.371
-And then -- and then --
So, you know, again,

00:05:06.371 --> 00:05:07.606
this is a two-hander,

00:05:07.606 --> 00:05:10.142
and smaller movies,
where everybody's like,

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:11.277
"Oh, my --"
You know, I remember

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.411
"Jackie Brown," for example.

00:05:12.411 --> 00:05:13.613
You're like, "Oh, my God.
Who's that guy?

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:14.681
That guy's great."

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.014
Stealing movies
with these little parts.

00:05:16.014 --> 00:05:18.050
And then, of course,
"Rush Hour" happens.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:19.685
-Yes.
-And this is another thing, man.

00:05:19.685 --> 00:05:21.253
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:22.688
-I was so excited, man,

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:24.957
because I knew that I could
put my comedy

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:27.893
with Jackie Chan's martial arts,
and it would be fantastic.

00:05:27.893 --> 00:05:30.730
But it's the 25th anniversary
of the first "Rush Hour."

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.731
-Unbelievable.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.731 --> 00:05:34.566
And, man, it don't --

00:05:34.566 --> 00:05:35.767
It seem a long time ago,

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:37.903
but Jackie
was so kind and so nice.

00:05:37.903 --> 00:05:39.238
He would give me a gift
every day

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.439
on the first "Rush Hour" set.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.041
He would send me over a gift,
a different gift.

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:43.943
I said, "Man, what is this?
Part of his culture?"

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:46.111
He's so nice.
Then I realized he's from China.

00:05:46.111 --> 00:05:48.247
They make everything over there,
he's getting it for free anyway.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.482
-Oh, that's very unfair.

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:51.050
-He wasn't paying for nothing.
-Oh, man.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.485
He's looking out the window,
like, "Look at Chris Tucker.

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:54.353
He gonna go broke
trying to keep up with me."

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:55.888
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.888 --> 00:05:57.924
"We make Jordan 1's in Taiwan."

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:59.758
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:01.761
-Speaking of Jordans, I want
to talk to you about "Air,"

00:06:01.761 --> 00:06:03.162
which you were fantastic in.

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:05.698
We're gonna be more
with Chris right after this.

